# The chargen primitives the owner has approved, and their route
# contracts.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR. A primitive is the C++ behind one step of the
# character-generation procedure. The procedure itself is data: a step
# in a seed names a primitive_ref, and the registry maps that name to a
# function. The registry also declares that step's legal exit labels,
# and a seed may route on those and no others.
#
# Name plus exits is the ROUTE CONTRACT, and it is what keeps the
# procedure data rather than code: a seed can rewire the flow, but only
# through doors the primitive opened. So the set of primitive names is
# a design surface. docs/RPG_MODULE.md OPEN item 1 says new ones
# surface for the owner's approval rather than appearing as
# speculative engine vocabulary.
#
# WHY IT IS A FILE AND NOT A SENTENCE. The rule was written on
# 2026-08-09, when eight primitives existed. Seventeen exist now.
# Measured: not one of the nine additions was ever put in front of the
# owner. #59 added five in a single pull request. Nothing was harmed,
# and nothing noticed either, which is the same shape as every other
# finding this month: rank 0 grants cited and executed by nothing,
# relation endpoints validating nothing, a coverage sweep that never
# reached the aging table. A rule with no gate is an intention.
#
# HOW THE GATE WORKS. test_chargen compares this file against the live
# registry and fails when they differ, in either direction. It cannot
# stop a primitive being added; it makes the addition IMPOSSIBLE TO ADD
# QUIETLY, because the author must edit this file in the same commit
# and the diff says, in one line, that the procedure's vocabulary grew.
# That is a review trigger, not a permission system, and the difference
# is worth being honest about.
#
# FORMAT. One primitive per line: the name, a colon, then its route
# labels comma-separated and sorted. No labels means the step has no
# declared exits and always advances. Blank lines and # comments are
# ignored.
#
# TO ADD ONE: bring it to the owner first, with what the book's
# checklist step is and why an existing primitive will not carry it.
# Then add the line here in the same commit as the registry entry.

advance_term:
basic_training:
choose_career: finish
choose_term_end: continue,muster_out
draft_or_drifter: took_it
finish_character:
generate_characteristics:

# Approved 2026-08-15, retroactively, with the rest of this file.
# "You begin as a Rank 0 character." Twenty-three of the twenty-four
# careers print a grant in that row and nothing read it, so every
# generated character finished a skill level short of the book. The
# grant has to reach all 24 careers and only the rank-track table
# covers them, so it cannot ride the promotion step, which sees the 17
# careers with a commission or advancement row. Hence a step of its
# own. Shipped in 0.4.2 before this file existed.
grant_rank_zero:

